  story: 'THE SCOPE REVEAL (story v3, passed at the phase-1 gate) — structure AND\u2013BUT\u2013THEREFORE: AND a count beyond intuition is made auditable (one unit, one gate, one counted row — a measuring instrument at work) — BUT the count is one company\u2019s, and that company\u2019s own count of itself: the instrument\u2019s frame is the measure\u2019s boundary — THEREFORE the viewer knows precisely what the number is and what it is not: everything the frame does not cover stands outside the claim — not denied, not zeroed — present, alive, UNMEASURED. Planted question: \u201cWhose count is this — and what exactly does it cover?\u201d — planted by frame 1\u2019s empty seal-seat. Payoff: \u201calone\u201d (4.64–5.14) — the seal seated on \u201cGoogle\u201d, the owner named, the boundary understood. Named feeling: awe clarified. The antagonist is honestly ABSENT — a scope has none; THE NAMED TENSION is the gap between the count\u2019s scale and its frame. Climax: the reveal of scope completing on \u201calone\u201d at 5.14 s — 69% of the film. The tally is the declared CODA — the reveal\u2019s evidence, never a second peak. Sound-off reads of record — Scene 1: \u201can enormous golden count grows; beneath it a row of ten small units forms, streams through a gate, and settles inside it as one mark in a ring of twelve lights up on the gate — the month, come round again.\u201d Scene 2: \u201cthe count is swallowed, the gate stamps its own count GOOGLE, the light stops at the gate\u2019s edge and the world beyond it glows on dimly, uncounted; then tokens pass through the gate one by one and gather inside it — ten in all.\u201d',
